WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.700
The Last Ninja, battle your way to a showdown with the evil Shogun.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:30.160
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:31.440
I'm Mike.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:33.900
I'm Sean. And I'm Joe.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:40.020
And today we are playing the definitive experience of what would happen if the last ninja showed

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:41.180
up in Central Park.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:45.800
You say, like, what would happen if the last ninja would show up in Central Park?

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:49.760
Like, as if the last ninja is somebody we should know already.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:51.180
Who was the last ninja?

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:55.420
No, the last ninja is, it's like something that will become known to us.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.400
We, there are, there are currently many ninjas.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.280
We don't know who's going to be the last.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:10.900
This is the last ninja who apparently is like a 40 year old kind of pudgy dude that just lives in New York City.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.620
Or, or got teleported there.

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.500
Like, it's unclear how this game starts because it just throws you right into it.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:23.860
And you're like on this, you're on this box when, or like square when you start the game.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:27.760
And I thought that was like, oh, did he teleport here or something?

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.760
Like, is that what, is that what's going on?

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:33.400
Is that why a ninja is in New York City of all places?

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.940
In broad daylight. Right.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:41.020
Is that why the UI has his face and a really crude drawing of the Statue of Liberty on it?

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:42.980
Like, is, is that what's going on here?

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.260
But, all right, I guess I'll find out what's going on.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:48.740
First off, hard to figure out what this game is without the manual.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:54.520
Like, you can't just, this is not one where you can just be like, oh, I'll load up the ROM and start playing it.

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:56.580
It's like, you will not be able to start playing this game.

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:58.760
So, I've.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:00.400
No, sure, you can.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:01.700
Yeah, it's not illegal.

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:10.440
Like, like it is to be an, it is illegal to juggle milk bottles and throw them at ninjas in Central Park.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:12.020
That is a known illegal thing.

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:26.400
Here, though, the problem is, is that if you do something like that, you might have an experience similar to mine where you leave that room and get to the next room and get into a fist fight with somebody who has unlimited HP.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:28.060
Like, you can't actually kill them.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.820
You can just only incapacitate them.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:32.500
But maybe that's because that's like the ninja code or something.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.180
And then there's this button on a wall.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:38.380
And, of course, you want to punch that button.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:39.520
Like, it's just, it's natural.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:49.400
So, I did the, I did the puzzle solving thing and I punched the button and it closed in and I could not for the life of me figure out what to do next.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:03:00.000
Because for some reason, my peanut sized brain couldn't think to go back to the other, only other room I'd ever been in in this game so far and be like, oh, I wonder if anything's different in there.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.240
I didn't do that.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:07.900
I never thought to do that for the 10 minutes that I was like then online and everything.

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:09.600
And I was like, what is this game even?

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:10.500
I was reading the manual.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:20.220
And eventually I just watched a long play and said, oh, that room with the square that I thought was where you teleported from is actually outlined for a trap door.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:22.060
Yeah. And that's how you start the game.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:28.580
So, that's when you realized that you are playing basically a point and click adventure game with extra steps.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:39.380
And, again, like I think the craziest part about this game just is the whole scenario.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:46.800
Like you just are, you just are this ninja in modern day New York City.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.080
There are no other ninjas.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:52.520
There's no, there's no like league of ninjas.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:54.100
You're just the ninja.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:55.620
Well, you're the last one.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:58.180
Why would there be a league? Well, I mean, I guess you're right.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:59.960
You're right. That is in the title.

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:03.980
But it's still like inexplicable that you are a ninja.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:05.560
Yeah, right, right.

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:14.160
And it's all just these kind of like goofy situations, like puzzles that you have to solve.

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:21.960
And, yeah, but it's more so because for a game that has so, like there is fighting.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:25.900
Like you do, like Mike was saying, you do incapacitate a guy.

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:28.280
You can also just try and avoid them.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:32.440
So, there is some like press this button to attack.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:34.640
But they made two attack buttons.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:41.100
And then you, and this is why you can't really get too far in this game without looking at a manual.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:47.700
Is because you immediately have to start like pressing button combinations just to like get stuff out of your inventory.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.100
And it's just very strange.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:54.000
Yeah, I mean, I don't even think a manual is enough for me.

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:56.440
I need a guide. Because I needed like this.

00:04:56.540 --> 00:05:00.200
It's just the point and click adventure-ness of it.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:05.220
And my brain cannot separate that from like all the shit I've got to do with this ninja at the time.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:10.820
So, like I'm not, I'm just focusing on like getting this ninja to like move where I wanted to move and to attack.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.840
So, then when I like get to the places, I'm like, I don't know.

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:17.580
I wasn't paying attention to what's on the, you know, where the button is or whatever.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:21.580
So, I needed a guide to even get anywhere in this.

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:28.040
But like, luckily, I will say that you mentioned that you could try to avoid people.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:29.820
You don't even have to try that hard.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:34.620
They don't really, you know, they don't really bother you if you don't bother them for the most part.

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:39.320
I guess it depends on how lucky you get with like wherever they spawn or something.

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:41.140
Because they will block you.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:48.920
And then you look like an idiot or at least I look like an idiot just jumping in place trying to get past these guys.

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:50.840
Oh, yeah, yeah. You can get like cornered.

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:54.280
Yeah. For sure. Yeah.

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:59.460
So, but like if you just like don't engage with them from the very beginning, a lot of them are just like standing there.

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:00.480
Some of them do come at you.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:12.900
But even when you are in a fight, what drove me crazy is like there's just nothing about these punches and kicks or anything about the way you're playing this game that makes you feel like a ninja.

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:17.800
Like all the way back in like Kung Fu, you felt like cool when you were doing your kicks.

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:23.340
Like this is just like it feels like I'm just standing there like, all right, like I got to position myself like right here so I can throw the punch right there.

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:24.980
Okay. And now he's going to hit me a couple of times.

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.160
Oh, I got to move over like one inch so I can kick.

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:30.960
And like it's just like it feels like it doesn't feel good.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:33.420
It feels like I'm playing as myself.

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:36.200
Like if I dressed up in a costume.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:40.880
And that's largely because of the isometric viewpoint, which we haven't brought up yet.

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:43.500
But this game is another isometric game.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:53.160
And like that's what's making this so much weirder to navigate because I don't disagree with the point and click like analogy.

00:06:54.020 --> 00:07:07.060
But because this isn't a game where like you use a mouse and like pick up objects and have like clear commands because you're also like in a in an actual action game at the same time.

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:18.720
Any kind of like combination of items or puzzle solving on top of being the character at the same time creates a very frustrating experience.

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:27.580
Most of the times for actually solving the puzzles because like there's puzzles in games that are just basically like try to find the key so that you can open the door.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:29.360
And sometimes the key is just on the ground.

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:33.080
Other times it's like a combination or something like this game has stuff like that.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:37.560
But then it also has like, OK, jump on this boat.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:40.380
Yeah, exactly. Don't even jump on this boat.

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:42.360
How do you get the boat to move first?

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:50.120
Well, you have to jump over this area of water that leads to another another screen.

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:52.560
So you have to know that there's going to be water there in the first place.

00:07:52.680 --> 00:08:06.120
You have to jump from the other screen to then make a leap of faith to the next screen over so that you're in the jumping animations that you land in the little island and then take your stick, which you hopefully acquire because if you don't have the stick, you can't do this.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:16.200
And then nudge the boat and then the boat starts moving and then you go back to screens to where the boat is going to line up to line up your jump to land on the boat as it's sailing across.

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:19.200
It's like, I mean, damn, pretty cool puzzle.

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:23.000
Like it is involved, but like it's really hard to pull off.

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:29.580
You will die trying to jump on the first boat many, many times before you get to that second.

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:31.280
Like, why can't ninjas swim?

00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:35.220
I mean, it's a well-known fact that.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:36.980
Yeah. Ninjas can't swim.

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:40.660
Right. That's why there's only one left.

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:43.560
Yeah, they all drowned.

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:45.520
Since the floods.

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:49.760
Yeah. Joe, you mentioned that you don't feel like a ninja in this game.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:50.600
And it is true.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:56.840
Like, I agree with Sean that, or maybe both of you said this, that like you can't avoid the enemies.

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:59.480
You should avoid the enemies because they can't be knocked out.

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:03.180
So you're going to keep going back to these screens anyway, and you do have a health bar and such.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:06.060
So you might as well avoid conflict when possible.

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:13.940
So I guess in a way, the game is forcing you to be non-violent or maybe a little stealthy, but it should have went more in on the stealth.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:15.840
Wait, it should have went in on the stealth.

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:23.640
You're a ninja. Like, what are you doing just walking around in broad daylight in Central Park and everybody's just like, yeah, this guy here again.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:33.500
Well, and, you know, I don't want to rule out the fact that, like, the gameplay being, like, you not feeling like a ninja might have been, like, tongue in cheek.

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:36.480
You know, it might have been, like, yeah, you're the last ninja, and, like, look at this guy.

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:38.120
He's an idiot. He's walking around in broad daylight.

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:40.240
He looks like he's in, like, a Halloween costume.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:43.480
But, like, I don't think it's that crazy.

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:49.980
I mean, the opening, like, intro screen made me think, oh, this is going to be a silly game, and it's, like, intended to be a comedy.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:55.260
Now, I didn't really get that while playing it, but, like, when I'm looking back right now at the game, I'm like, it really is.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:10:01.780
It's like the little, like, bamboo font and the music with, like, and the Fred and Wilma or whatever are the, like, high scores.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:11.980
Yeah, wait, wait, we got to talk about the high scores for a second because it is funny that it is Bert and Ernie as first and second place.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:13.660
Then Barney and Fred.

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:17.540
So, we have Sesame Street and the Flintstones.

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:25.800
Then it's Stan and Oliver, which is Stan Laurel and Oliver Hardy, two old-style comedians.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:29.800
Yes. And then it just turns into Hello Marco and Rex.

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:31.860
Rex, like, well, who the hell are they?

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:37.420
Whoever Marco and Rex are just got immortalized next to some pretty important names.

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:39.260
I'm trying to think it's their cats.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:42.220
Hello, our cats.

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:49.000
Yeah. I think that there's definitely, that definitely leads me to believe that some of this is supposed to be funny.

00:10:49.180 --> 00:10:53.460
But a lot of this, like, I just, I can't see that they did this on purpose.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:11:01.260
Like, when you pick up an item, did anybody else just think he was just sort of, like, squatting on it and, like, picking it up with his butt?

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:05.320
Am I the only one that immediately jumped to this?

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:06.140
No, no, not at all.

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:07.780
Okay. Just making sure.

00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:09.560
I think the game gets silly like that all the time, though.

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:15.360
Like, there's that, there's a crocodile blocking the exit out of the sewers.

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:18.820
And naturally, what would you do?

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:20.720
You would set the crocodile on fire.

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:26.180
Yes. You just throw a Molotov cocktail at it and the next thing you know, it's on fire and you're out of that room.

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:35.720
Much like how ninjas can't swim, we do know that, like, the moral enemy of any crocodile is a Molotov cocktail.

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:37.700
Right, or just fire in general.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:46.180
I've always said that, like, one of the scariest days of my life was when I was at Universal Theme Park and I was on the Jaws ride.

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:52.540
And it was scary enough having, you know, a mechanical Jaws shark coming after you on the boat.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:12:00.140
But then at one point, the river that you're on, on the boat cruise, it lights on fire.

00:12:00.140 --> 00:12:02.540
And I found out that you can have fire in water.

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:06.240
And I was like, oh my God, like, we are so, like, this is possible?

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:10.900
Like, all of our worst fears are being realized if you could have fire on top of water.

00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:14.580
But that's when, that's only when the crocodiles harness that power.

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:16.300
Like, usually they don't have that.

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:17.400
Look it up, people.

00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:18.720
Fire on water.

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:39.940
Scary stuff. All right, so the hook of this game, you know, whether it's the tone or the ridiculousness or being a ninja, the real game is about figuring out what object you need, where to use it, and how to position yourself so that the game understands that you're trying to use it.

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:42.980
Because so much of this is, like, contextual.

00:12:43.180 --> 00:12:52.100
And I do think, like, if it was a, even followed more of the point and click commands and had, like, a, when you're near, let's say you're near a chest, right?

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:54.300
I don't even think there are chests in this game.

00:12:54.500 --> 00:13:01.120
But if there was, and you were able to then, like, navigate to a submenu for use and then key.

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:08.920
Like, that would be better than having to cycle through this menu of just, your UI says you're using and you're holding.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:15.460
And using is, like, what you're using to attack and you're holding is the item that you're trying to use to solve the puzzle.

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:19.040
It's just all a very, like, clunky experience.

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:28.060
And when, and this is something I never truly understood, like, you always kind of default to using a ninja kicking.

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:33.160
And there's always, like, a number next to that.

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:34.560
What does that mean?

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.560
Do you know how many kicks you have left?

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:44.620
Yeah, I thought that that was just, like, they ran out of real estate on this UI because of their giant ninja head in Statue of Liberty.

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:50.960
So they just, like, had the using thing, but then, like, when you're done selecting it, it switches back to, like, oh, and this is how many lives you have.

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:52.160
Okay. I thought it was lives.

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:54.400
But I don't know. And, yeah, this is so strange.

00:13:55.480 --> 00:14:03.980
And then I started to think that, like, do you lose the item you were holding if you pick up another one?

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:06.520
Or is it just, like, you've got to start cycling through it again?

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:11.980
Because I ended up, like, just dying so many times I could never really keep track of what my inventory ever was.

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:18.880
But I remember, like, I picked up a key, and I needed to use that key to open up a gate.

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:26.900
But then I tried as hard as I could to find that key, and I accidentally picked up, like, an egg muffin since.

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:30.600
And I'm like, did I overwrite my key?

00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:34.280
You're not thinking of the right button inputs, Sean.

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:37.320
It's not simply enough to use select to cycle through them.

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:41.600
You have to press select and the A button to cycle through what you're holding.

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:42.940
It's so crazy.

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:47.340
Because to cycle through what you're using, it's select and the B button.

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:51.580
These are just normal things that everybody's come to understand in video games.

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:56.860
We always cycle through our inventories with the select and B button and vice versa, with the A button.

00:14:57.260 --> 00:14:58.640
It's tough. It's very tough.

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:05.620
I also don't like some of the, like, holding and then, like, just showing the picture of, like, the world's worst cheeseburger.

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:07.160
What is that?

00:15:07.160 --> 00:15:10.680
That actually looks like two pancakes with, like, some jam stuffed between them.

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:11.680
That doesn't look like a cheeseburger.

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:13.900
It's a New York-style cheeseburger, Mike.

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:16.820
Or it's actually, sorry, it's just a hamburger, according to the manual.

00:15:16.820 --> 00:15:18.080
And this is where things get weird.

00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:22.100
It has this thing about clues about objects, right?

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:25.520
And it tells you, like, it's not telling you exactly what they're for or whatever.

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:31.920
But for hamburger, it just has in quotes, as if, like, somebody, like, your mentor said this to you.

00:15:32.340 --> 00:15:39.000
Greater love hath no man than this, that he lay down his extra hamburger for a friend.

00:15:39.440 --> 00:15:42.240
Okay, no, this is all definitely on purpose now.

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:47.080
Right. And so hamburgers, you use them to get an extra life.

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:49.160
I see, yes.

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:53.340
So, you know, you go through all this.

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:56.000
I feel like we've touched on how you interact with the world.

00:15:58.160 --> 00:16:02.840
This all leads us to learn that it's all Satanists, right?

00:16:04.220 --> 00:16:05.600
Is that what was going on?

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:09.280
Well, you get into... There is some cult thing going on.

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:14.520
Yeah, you get into this mansion, and then you just see a pentagram on the ground.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:17.060
And you have to...

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:20.100
You do something with a safe.

00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:22.540
I guess you picked up a combination at some point.

00:16:22.900 --> 00:16:24.160
I didn't get this far.

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:27.180
Oh, I actually didn't get this far either.

00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:30.660
Now I'm seeing it. Yeah, the pentagram even, like, comes to life and shit.

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:32.740
Like, oh, it's... Yeah, that's pretty spooky.

00:16:32.960 --> 00:16:34.300
You unlock the safe.

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:37.680
